 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**No, the Aussie dollar is strong against the yen right now, not weak.**\n\n- **Latest:** A$1 bought about **¥109.67** on 16 October 2026 (RBA 4pm rate, the latest daily figure).\n- **A year ago:** about ¥100.84 at end-October 2025, so the Aussie has gained roughly 9% against the yen over the past year.\n- **Recent trend:** it peaked around ¥114.3 in April 2026 and has eased since. It was ¥114.6 on 1 September and ¥109.5 at the end of September, and has held in the ¥109–111 range through October.\n- **Longer view:** the yen was much weaker in mid-2025, when the Aussie fell to about ¥91.4 in April 2025.\n\nA higher number means the Aussie buys more yen, so the yen has been the weaker currency over the past year. The recent dip from April's high is a modest pullback, not a sign of Aussie weakness against the yen.",
